@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Introduction to C#";
}

<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
<p>
    C# (pronounced "C-Sharp") is a modern, object-oriented programming language developed by Microsoft.
    It is designed for building a wide range of enterprise applications that run on the .NET Framework.
    C# is known for its simplicity, versatility, and strong type safety.
</p>
<h2>Key Features of C#</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)</li>
    <li>Strong Type Safety</li>
    <li>Garbage Collection</li>
    <li>Interoperability with other .NET languages</li>
</ul>
<h2>Getting Started with C#</h2>
<p>
    To get started with C#, you need a code editor like Visual Studio or Visual Studio Code.
    C# programs are typically compiled using the .NET Core or .NET Framework runtime.
</p>
